OL,3,GNEWSACrime gang's 30 skips of waste    
OL,4,Acleared from street                    
OL,6,FThirty skips' worth of waste have been 
OL,7,Fcleared from a town centre street,     
OL,8,Fwhich was used by an organised crime   
OL,9,Fgang to store and burn rubbish, a      
OL,10,Freport has found.                      
OL,12,FAn Environmental Enforcement report    
OL,13,Fsaid the rubbish in Roper Street,      
OL,14,FKeighley, had lead to vermin           
OL,15,Finfestations and much of the waste had 
OL,16,Fbeen illegally burned on site.         
OL,18,FAccording to the report, which was     
OL,19,Fpresented to Bradford Council's        
OL,20,FKeighley Area Committee this week, the 
OL,21,Forganised crime group had now left the 
OL,22,Fpremises.                              
OL,23,APub: 26-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2 
